<p>Sounds are created and packaged using the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/FMOD" title="FMOD">FMOD</a> tool. This is a third-party tool that is included with the Dragon Age toolset. See the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/FMOD" title="FMOD">FMOD</a> page for documentation on how to use it to create sound resources for use in the designer toolkit.
</p><p>The designer toolset is our way to get sounds into the game. In this application we can define the sound design for any particular area in the game. We have the ability to draw audio volumes to define certain areas, assign sounds to them and even modify and mix within the volume itself, in real time. We can drop emitters for our 3D sounds and modify them as well.
</p><p>Voice over is handled separately by the toolset; see the relevant section of <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Conversation" title="Conversation">conversation</a> for more details.
</p>
